The derived implementation is distributed under the BSD 3-Clause terms in
LICENSES/NumPy-BSD-3-Clause.txt. Preserve this notice and the accompanying license
when redistributing the derived implementation. The enclosing crate's MIT license
does not replace these terms.

MathProfile::NumpySimd evaluates that formula with portable Rust f32 arithmetic
and scalar fused multiply-add; no CPU intrinsics or external runtime dependency
is required. MathProfile::Libm uses the platform scalar exponential. NumPy's
float32 CPU dispatch can produce different rounded intermediate results across
these profiles. Bindings should select the profile using the installed NumPy
build's capability/dispatch metadata; do not infer universal parity from one
platform's frozen fixtures. Native default selection uses x86 AVX2 plus FMA
hardware capability and otherwise selects the scalar profile. Compiled NumPy
dispatch availability and disabled CPU features may require an explicit override.

The guarded AVX512 float32 atan2 kernel vendors Intel SVML assembly from the
NumPy/SVML repository at commit bd9d46e0c627ab16f3d2641f7cdb1bc15d303ba4:
https://github.com/numpy/SVML/tree/bd9d46e0c627ab16f3d2641f7cdb1bc15d303ba4

The assembly retains its Copyright (C) 2023 Intel Corporation and BSD-3-Clause
SPDX header. The repository also carries Copyright (c) 2005-2021, NumPy
Developers. Both notices and the BSD-3-Clause conditions are reproduced in
LICENSES/Intel-SVML-BSD-3-Clause.txt. Preserve that file and the source header.
This kernel reproduces NumPy's dispatched float32 intermediates. The Rust core
assembles the bundled source through LLVM; no external C/C++ compiler or
Python runtime is required. Runtime capability checks guard its private entry.
